### orderflow demo requests (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client)
# Prerequisites: docker compose up -d, then start order-service (port 8081).
# Day 2 scope: orders are accepted and stay PENDING. The saga paths are added from Day 6.

@orderService = http://localhost:8081
@customerId = 2ceecac6-e0e2-4ce0-a0da-f1edfb0b3893
@idempotencyKey = demo-key-001

### 1. Place an order -> 202 Accepted, status PENDING
# @name placeOrder
POST {{orderService}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "currency": "EUR",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "MUG-RED", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": "12.50" },
    { "sku": "TEA-GREEN", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": "8.00" }
  ]
}

### 2. Read it back (polling target for the saga outcome)
GET {{orderService}}/orders/{{placeOrder.response.body.orderId}}

### 3. Retry with the same key and an equivalent body -> 202, same orderId, Idempotent-Replayed: true
POST {{orderService}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "currency": "EUR",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "MUG-RED", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": "12.5" },
    { "sku": "TEA-GREEN", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": "8" }
  ]
}

### 4. Reuse the key for a different order -> 422 Idempotency key reused
POST {{orderService}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "currency": "EUR",
  "lines": [ { "sku": "MUG-RED", "quantity": 5, "unitPrice": "12.50" } ]
}

### 5. Break several rules at once -> 400 with every violation listed
POST {{orderService}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-invalid-001

{
  "currency": "XYZ",
  "lines": [ { "sku": "MUG-RED", "quantity": 0, "unitPrice": "-1" } ]
}
